---
// Converted from the demo page src/pages/security/index.html — content unchanged.
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Navigation from '../../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Dialogs from '../../components/Dialogs.astro';
import Seo from '../../components/Seo.astro';
import { css, js } from '../../lib/site';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff">
<title>Security — Favorite Hearts</title>
<meta name="description" content="How Favorite Hearts protects your information, what our badges mean, how to keep your account safe, and how to report a security issue.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href={css("landing.css")}>
<script is:inline src={js("site-config.js")} defer>
</script>
<script is:inline src={js("site.js")} defer>
</script>
<script is:inline src={js("resource-carousel.js")} defer>
</script>
<script is:inline src={js("resources.js")} defer>
</script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href={css("monochrome.css")}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href={css("resources.css")}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href={css("welcome.css")}>
<script is:inline src={js("welcome.js")} defer>
</script>
<script is:inline src={js("motion.js")} defer></script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href={css("design-system.css")}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href={css("tailwind.css")}>
<Seo route="/security/" title={"Security — Favorite Hearts"} description={"How Favorite Hearts protects your information, what our badges mean, how to keep your account safe, and how to report a security issue."} headline={"A little care. A safer connection."} />
</head>
<body class="tw-antialiased">
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<Header />
<Navigation />
<main id="main" class="resource-page" data-theme="light">
<section class="section resource-intro">
<p class="label">Security</p>
<h1>A little care.<br>A safer connection.</h1>
<p class="resource-lead">Protect your information, recognise suspicious requests, and know where to turn if something feels wrong.</p>
</section>
<section class="section resource-section">
<p class="label">Good habits, from the start</p>
<h2>Keep your information<br>in your hands.</h2>
<div class="security-carousel" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Security habits">
<div class="principles-track" tabindex="0" aria-label="Security habits. Use left and right arrow keys to browse.">
<article class="principle">
<span class="principle-number">01</span>
<h3>Keep access private</h3>
<p>Never share a sign-in code or a password with anyone: Favorite Hearts staff will never ask for them. Sign out of shared devices.</p>
</article>
<article class="principle">
<span class="principle-number">02</span>
<h3>Check before you click</h3>
<p>Be cautious with unexpected links, downloads, or requests to sign in. Open the website yourself when you are unsure who sent a message.</p>
</article>
<article class="principle">
<span class="principle-number">03</span>
<h3>Share only what is needed</h3>
<p>Keep identity documents, financial details, and private contact information out of public profiles and social comments.</p>
</article>
</div>
<div class="principle-controls">
<div class="review-indicators principle-dashes" aria-hidden="true">
<span class="active">
</span>
<span>
</span>
<span>
</span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section resource-band" data-theme="dark">
<p class="label">How we protect it</p>
<h2>Trust should be informed.</h2>
<p>Identity documents, receipts and original photos are kept in private storage and shown only through links that expire within minutes, to people allowed to see them. Identity documents are deleted 90 days after our review. Members who may not see a photo receive a separate blurred copy. Staff sign in with two-step login, sign-in and code attempts are limited, and a bot check guards the sign-in forms. Still, a badge is never a promise that a connection is risk-free.</p>
<a class="resource-link" href="/privacy/">Read our Privacy Policy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</a>
</section>
<section class="section resource-section resource-split">
<div>
<p class="label">Report a technical concern</p>
<h2>Spotted something<br>that isn’t right?</h2>
<p>If you notice a suspicious link, possible data exposure, or a weakness in the website, tell us privately.</p>
<a class="pill" href="mailto:hello@favoritehearts.com?subject=Security%20report">Report a security issue</a>
</div>
<div class="report-guidance">
<h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
<rect x="5" y="4" width="14" height="17" rx="2"/>
<path d="M9 4V2h6v2M9 9h6M9 13h6M9 17h4"/>
</svg>What to include</h3>
<ol>
<li>The page address and a short description.</li>
<li>What you expected and what happened instead.</li>
<li>Your device, browser, and the approximate time.</li>
<li>A screenshot with private information hidden, if useful.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section resource-section">
<p class="label">Security questions</p>
<h2>A few useful answers.</h2>
<div class="resource-questions">
<details name="resource-answer">
<summary>Someone asked for my password or code. What should I do?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div>
<p>Do not share it: Favorite Hearts staff will never ask for a password or a sign-in code. If you already shared a code, tell us straight away so we can help you secure your account, and tell us if the message claimed to be from Favorite Hearts.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details name="resource-answer">
<summary>Does HTTPS mean a person or payment request is trustworthy?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div>
<p>No. An encrypted connection helps protect traffic in transit, but it does not prove that a person is genuine or that a request is safe. Check the website address and independently confirm unexpected requests.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details name="resource-answer">
<summary>Is a verification badge a guarantee of safety?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div>
<p>No. Each badge means one specific check was done: an identity document reviewed by our staff and a phone verified by SMS (“Manager verified”, “Candidate identity verified”), or a candidate confirming their own profile (“Candidate confirmed”). It is not a government verification, and no badge can guarantee someone’s intentions or future behaviour.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details name="resource-answer">
<summary>Where do I raise a concern about another person?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
</summary>
<div>
<p>Use Report on their profile in the app, and see our <a href="/trust-and-safety/">Trust &amp; Safety guidance</a>. If there is immediate danger, contact local emergency services rather than waiting for a reply from us.</p>
</div>
</details>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section resource-end" data-theme="dark">
<div>
<p class="label">Let’s keep it thoughtful</p>
<h2>Questions about<br>your information?</h2>
<p>We can help you find the right next step for a privacy or security enquiry.</p>
</div>
<div class="resource-actions">
<a class="pill" href="/help/">Explore Help &amp; FAQ <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</a>
<a class="pill" href="/contact/">Contact us <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</a>
<p class="response-hours">Daily, 8:00 AM–10:00 PM<br>Sri Lanka time</p>
</div>
</section>
</main><Footer />
<Dialogs />
</body>
</html>
